  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> rests on another block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and is tied to a wall as shown in the figure. The coefficient of friction between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and that between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and ground is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The minimum force required to move the block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0017_54bbaf1a05e4.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 129px;\" /></p>"
